WEBVTT

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:06.940
In a Jet Race,

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:13.400
the Jetter and the Shooter come together as one

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:17.660
to soar with the wind and speed across the water
in the world's most intense aquatic sport!

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.020
Misa-chan!

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:22.010
Namiki Rin of Asakusa Girls' High School!

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:25.410
She's gone on the offensive with an
extraordinary starting dash!

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:28.620
Allow me to give a quick rundown of the course.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:29.580
Tee-hee!

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:35.220
Today's race begins near the mouth of
the Kandagawa at Yanagibashi.

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:36.840
The course doubles back at Hijiribashi,

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:40.970
and our contenders must complete a total of three laps.

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:45.340
You're awfully giddy for someone
in the middle of a race.

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:47.140
Or have you forgotten?!

00:02:56.920 --> 00:03:00.220
Oh no! There's been a sudden suit purge!

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:01.720
Resident expert, Syoco-senpai!

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:05.630
For those who are new to Jet Racing,
give us the lowdown on the suits' purging function!

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:13.130
When the suits that our contenders are wearing absorb
the harsh impact from a water gun, for example,

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:15.800
they are designed to purge themselves
as a type of safety feature.

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:17.550
A safety feature?! I see!

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:19.420
A safety feature?

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:21.090
A safety feature.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:27.720
The fact that her suit purged itself after only two blows
indicates she was shot with pinpoint accuracy.

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:30.800
Misa-chan! Is your butt okay?!

00:03:30.970 --> 00:03:31.970
I'm fine.

00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:32.970
Are you sure?!

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:33.970
I said I'm fine!

00:03:33.970 --> 00:03:35.220
What about your poor butt?!

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:36.840
Don't worry about it!
Just pay attention!

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:40.510
Although it's quite common to purge
an opposing Shooter's suit

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:43.800
while trying to suppress their attacks.

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:48.010
Oh! Could this be her way of saying that
the battle's just getting started?!

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:52.880
You're going to regret thinking you could
let your guard down around Kuromaru Manpuku!

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:59.970
As you can see, the Shooter takes aim and
fires at the machine's damage targets.

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:06.340
The damage targets are situated
along various areas of the machine's frame,

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:09.590
and taking a blow to these areas
will generate a shockwave.

00:04:09.590 --> 00:04:12.970
Negatively affecting the performance of
the opposing team's machine!

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:18.380
In addition, each damage target is worth
a certain number of points.

00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:22.220
The more difficult it is to hit the target,
the more points it's worth.

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:27.420
When the number of damage points received by
a machine reaches a particular threshold,

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:30.090
the output of its drive becomes temporarily restricted.

00:04:30.550 --> 00:04:32.340
This is called the "Power Cut System."

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:35.510
In other words, the machine is forcibly slowed down!

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:37.090
Exactly.

00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:39.420
Speed can be the deciding factor in a match,

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:42.880
so taking advantage of this system is the key to victory.

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:50.880
The Tamakaze has taken damage,
but that doesn't seem to be affecting its performance!

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:55.130
Its frame has considerable weight,
making it safer and sturdier than average.

00:04:55.130 --> 00:04:58.630
I've heard that the Tamakaze's drive
is what makes it so heavy!

00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:01.510
It's equipped with a drive capable of
putting out significant power,

00:05:01.510 --> 00:05:05.010
leaving it at a disadvantage in terms
of maneuverability and rounding corners.

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:07.880
But as I said earlier, it's safe, durable,

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:10.300
and accelerates faster than any other
on the straightaways.

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:21.590
Take this!

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:24.920
They've pulled ahead!

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:27.720
Musashino Girls' High School has
turned the tide in their favor!

00:05:28.420 --> 00:05:30.510
Musa Girls' victories follow a pattern.

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:34.420
They start out slow,
but once the Tamakaze's drive kicks into gear,

00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:37.720
they pick up speed and
blow straight past their opponents.

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:46.260
On the other hand, Namiki's Orcano is more balanced

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:47.450
and reliable in all sorts of situations.

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:49.550
It's easily maneuverable,

00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:51.990
ideal for closing the gap on corners, but...

00:05:55.340 --> 00:05:58.800
Shijuin rounds the corner with the skill
and finesse of a professional!

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:03.170
Oh no! Namiki swerves wildly towards
the outer edge of the river!

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:12.090
Shijuin's ability to navigate those corners
is almost hypnotic to watch!

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:17.720
The ease with which she pilots the Tamakaze is
truly remarkable for a high school student.

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:25.260
I highly doubt Namiki will be able
to make up for lost time!

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:26.760
Not so fast.

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:28.880
On a course with this many straightaways,

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:34.050
the fact that she's managed to keep up despite
the difference in their machines' power is impressive.

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:35.260
I see!

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:38.410
Though relatively unknown,
Namiki is a force to be reckoned with!

00:06:55.050 --> 00:06:59.550
Namiki narrows the gap on the turn,
but she's left in the dust on the straightaway!

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:22.500
Try as she might,
Asa Girls' Namiki Rin struggles to catch up!

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:25.210
I expected her to trail farther behind
on the straightaways.

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:26.590
Our contenders are approaching

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:28.630
the Hijiribashi turnaround point for the second time!

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:34.420
Now!

00:07:34.970 --> 00:07:36.170
What'd she say?!

00:07:41.550 --> 00:07:44.420
The Orcano overtakes the Tamakaze on the inside!

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:47.260
I did it!

00:07:47.420 --> 00:07:51.420
A surprising turn of events,
gaining ground on Shijuin of all people.

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:54.420
No!

00:07:58.010 --> 00:07:59.880
All that trouble for nothing...

00:08:01.800 --> 00:08:03.420
What am I doing?

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:14.130
It seems you're finally taking this seriously.

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:16.840
At least now I won't be bored to death!

00:08:20.510 --> 00:08:23.760
Uh-oh, an intense shooting match has broken out!

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:29.510
A gun's water supply cannot be
replenished during a race.

00:08:29.510 --> 00:08:32.420
Efficiency and accuracy can spell
either victory or defeat.

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:38.670
We've reached the final lap of the race!

00:08:38.670 --> 00:08:40.840
The winner will be decided by this last stretch!

00:08:40.840 --> 00:08:44.090
The Tamakaze swoops through the
inside of the turn this time!

00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:49.220
I'm surprised that both teams have refrained
from utilizing the boost function thus far.

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:52.760
Syoco-senpai, please explain
the importance of the boost function!

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:57.510
A boost charges the machine's
drive energy while in motion.

00:08:57.510 --> 00:09:01.470
Once a certain amount of energy has built up,
it's released all at once,

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:05.550
providing a temporary,
yet substantial, increase in power.

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:10.260
Shijuin has only ever used the
boost function twice in an official match!

00:09:10.260 --> 00:09:13.010
In some circles, she's called the "Boostless Queen"!

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:17.220
It seems she avoids using a boost in races
she believes can be won without it.

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:22.380
In fact, she's never lost an official match
as a result of her hesitance to use a boost.

00:09:22.870 --> 00:09:26.660
Meanwhile, Namiki continues to show
no sign of using a boost either!

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:28.630
What in the world is going on here?!

00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:31.590
Why doesn't she use a boost?

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:33.510
Is she trying to upstage me?

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:36.800
She has no idea who she's dealing with!

00:09:40.170 --> 00:09:42.170
Here comes the last turn!

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:51.340
Incredible!

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:54.170
Namiki swoops in from the outside this time!

00:09:55.170 --> 00:09:58.380
She's completely overtaken the Tamakaze!

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:16.550
Strong on those straightaways,

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:19.470
the Tamakaze catches up to the Orcano
and pushes forward!

00:10:23.010 --> 00:10:26.390
Musa Girls' pulls ahead!
But Asa Girls' refuses to back down!

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:31.840
They've passed Mikurahashi Bridge.

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:34.050
It's the last spurt!

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:46.670
What?!

00:10:47.090 --> 00:10:50.590
Oh no! It appears Kuromaru's suit has been purged!

00:10:50.590 --> 00:10:53.090
And the Orcano steals the lead!

00:10:58.470 --> 00:11:00.340
That was a great race!

00:11:05.380 --> 00:11:06.590
Damn it!

00:11:09.300 --> 00:11:10.510
Take this!

00:11:15.260 --> 00:11:17.920
Wh-What?! No way!

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:25.760
Goal!

00:11:26.380 --> 00:11:28.970
Asakusa Girls' High School put forth a valiant effort,

00:11:28.970 --> 00:11:32.090
but it was the dynamic duo of
Shijuin Kaguya and Manpuku Kuromaru

00:11:32.090 --> 00:11:35.710
from Musashino Girls' High School
who achieved victory!

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:40.050
Manpuku appeared quite calm as
she delivered the final blow.

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:45.090
She realized that the damage from her next shot
would reach the Power Cut threshold.

00:11:45.090 --> 00:11:48.220
Which means she was confident in
her ability to hit the mark, right?

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:49.420
Exactly.

00:11:59.420 --> 00:12:00.630
Namiki...

00:12:02.630 --> 00:12:04.630
I had so much fun!

00:12:04.630 --> 00:12:06.050
What about you, Misa-chan?!

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:23.050
I...

00:12:28.090 --> 00:12:29.510
S-Sorry!

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:32.010
Kind of unseemly, huh?

00:12:32.010 --> 00:12:35.720
I remember my mom doing it a lot when I was little.

00:12:36.220 --> 00:12:38.630
It feels nice, though!

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:42.030
Namiki, why didn't you use a boost?

00:12:43.630 --> 00:12:45.670
Why didn't you use a boost?

00:12:48.420 --> 00:12:50.420
I didn't know how.

00:12:51.590 --> 00:12:56.090
That was the first time I've driven a jet ski with
a boost function, so I didn't know how.

00:12:56.420 --> 00:13:01.170
I'd only ever seen the old types of machines that
were popular back when my mom used to ride.

00:13:01.170 --> 00:13:05.670
So that's how you gave Shijuin a run for her money...

00:13:05.670 --> 00:13:07.090
Shijuin?

00:13:07.920 --> 00:13:10.380
Wait, do you mean that super gorgeous Jetter?!

00:13:10.380 --> 00:13:12.220
Shijuin Kaguya...

00:13:12.760 --> 00:13:16.920
Musashino Girls' High School is famous for
their Jet Racing, and she's their ace.

00:13:18.220 --> 00:13:20.630
Kaguya-san was amazing, wasn't she?!

00:13:20.630 --> 00:13:23.630
It was so cool how her suit and
her jet ski were both black!

00:13:23.630 --> 00:13:26.470
I can't wait to race her again someday...

00:13:31.420 --> 00:13:33.090
They're so lucky...

00:13:33.090 --> 00:13:34.970
This is their scheduled time slot.

00:13:34.970 --> 00:13:38.090
It was their turn to use the Kandagawa in the first place.

00:13:39.010 --> 00:13:42.760
Jet Racing clubs from many
different schools use the course,

00:13:42.760 --> 00:13:44.840
so they book time slots and take turns.

00:13:45.510 --> 00:13:50.260
Is that why they were so mean to us
when they told us to move?

00:13:50.260 --> 00:13:51.260
Yeah.

00:13:52.050 --> 00:13:53.880
What a relief!

00:13:53.880 --> 00:13:56.720
I'm not banned from the Kandagawa!

00:13:56.720 --> 00:13:57.800
Hey, listen!

00:13:57.800 --> 00:14:01.800
If we book our own time slot,
we get to use the course, right?!

00:14:02.130 --> 00:14:05.300
And then we could race together
as much as we want!

00:14:07.260 --> 00:14:11.470
Only the Jet Racing clubs recognized by the
Association are allowed to book a slot.

00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:14.380
They don't recognize our school?

00:14:14.380 --> 00:14:15.720
That's not the problem.

00:14:15.720 --> 00:14:17.590
We don't even have a Jet Racing Club.

00:14:17.590 --> 00:14:18.800
What?!

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:23.630
But this is the clubroom, isn't it?

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:25.590
It's, um...

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:29.340
No one else was using it, so I just...

00:14:31.050 --> 00:14:33.260
But what about the Orcano?

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:38.270
The school doesn't know what to do with it,
so it's just been sitting in the warehouse.

00:14:38.270 --> 00:14:39.670
Are you serious?!

00:14:49.590 --> 00:14:50.970
Aoi Misa...

00:14:50.970 --> 00:14:55.050
I finally found the opportunity to
challenge you to another race, and yet...

00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:31.420
Kandagawa...

00:15:31.420 --> 00:15:32.840
...Jet Girls!

00:15:47.010 --> 00:15:49.010
N-Namiki?!

00:15:49.010 --> 00:15:50.010
Misa-chan...

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:51.220
Wh-What is it?

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:52.760
I...

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:55.260
I'm going to start a Jet Racing Club!

00:15:57.420 --> 00:15:58.630
Why?

00:15:59.300 --> 00:16:03.170
I mean, the whole reason I came here
was to compete in Jet Races!

00:16:03.920 --> 00:16:06.130
So I'm going to start a Jet Racing Club!

00:16:12.050 --> 00:16:13.880
Sure, if that's what you want.

00:16:14.130 --> 00:16:15.340
Really?!

00:16:15.340 --> 00:16:16.550
I won't stop you.

00:16:19.550 --> 00:16:21.720
You're starting a Jet Racing Club?!

00:16:21.720 --> 00:16:22.720
Yeah!

00:16:22.720 --> 00:16:24.340
Today's the first day of practice.

00:16:24.340 --> 00:16:25.840
I'd be grateful for your help!

00:16:26.050 --> 00:16:27.970
H-Hold on a minute, Namiki-san!

00:16:27.970 --> 00:16:30.300
In order to start a club, there are certain procedures...

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:31.510
Okay!

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:36.510
First of all, you'll need at least five members and
a teacher who will act as your advisor-

00:16:36.510 --> 00:16:38.510
Five members and an advisor!

00:16:38.510 --> 00:16:42.550
A-A-And then, you'll need to fill out an application
with your names and a list of activities,

00:16:42.550 --> 00:16:46.760
submit it to the Student Council,
and receive their seal of approval...

00:16:47.220 --> 00:16:49.420
I'm counting on you, Yamada-sensei!

00:16:53.880 --> 00:16:56.300
You won't do it?

00:16:58.260 --> 00:16:59.550
I couldn't possibly!

00:16:59.550 --> 00:17:02.420
After all, I don't know a single thing about Jet Racing!

00:17:03.550 --> 00:17:04.760
That's alright!

00:17:04.760 --> 00:17:06.550
I'm plenty knowledgeable for the both of us!

00:17:06.550 --> 00:17:08.300
Th-That isn't the issue...

00:17:08.300 --> 00:17:12.920
As the club's advisor,
I'd be the one responsible for all its activities...

00:17:15.340 --> 00:17:17.760
Yamada-sensei!

00:17:21.880 --> 00:17:23.880
Thank you so much!

00:17:24.970 --> 00:17:27.300
It's for an adorable student...

00:17:27.300 --> 00:17:29.300
You can do it, Yamada!

00:17:30.760 --> 00:17:31.760
Please!

00:17:31.760 --> 00:17:33.010
I can't help you...

00:17:33.010 --> 00:17:37.760
If you join the club, I'll give you a piece of
my fried chicken every time we have it for dinner!

00:17:37.760 --> 00:17:38.760
What?!

00:17:38.760 --> 00:17:41.340
Do I seem like the type of person
to be swayed by food?!

00:17:41.340 --> 00:17:43.920
Then I'll give you a slice of my tonkatsu, too!

00:17:43.920 --> 00:17:47.420
Wh-Why do you keep acting like I'm
some sort of glutton?!

00:17:50.630 --> 00:17:51.840
Fine...

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:56.050
I don't know a whole lot about Jet Racing,
but I don't mind being a manager.

00:17:56.340 --> 00:17:57.590
Thank you!

00:17:57.590 --> 00:17:59.090
Calm down, Rin-chan...

00:17:59.090 --> 00:18:01.970
I'll give you half of my Hamburg steak to
show you how much I appreciate it!

00:18:01.970 --> 00:18:04.840
I'm the one who makes dinner, though.

00:18:39.920 --> 00:18:41.630
Oh, it's you, Coach!

00:18:42.380 --> 00:18:44.840
Good work, ladies.
Very admirable.

00:18:45.470 --> 00:18:47.670
We're only doing what comes naturally!

00:18:47.670 --> 00:18:49.510
I like that attitude.

00:18:50.380 --> 00:18:51.380
H-Hey!

00:18:51.380 --> 00:18:54.010
I see you've taken to snacking again.

00:18:54.010 --> 00:18:56.670
Make sure you keep a close eye on your weight.

00:18:56.670 --> 00:18:59.590
You're as relentless as ever, Coach.

00:19:07.220 --> 00:19:08.300
Hello there!

00:19:08.300 --> 00:19:09.510
Hot, hot, hot!

00:19:09.510 --> 00:19:10.130
Um-

00:19:10.130 --> 00:19:11.340
Excuse me!

00:19:11.340 --> 00:19:15.050
It's extremely rude to enter a room
without knocking first, you know!

00:19:21.050 --> 00:19:22.260
Hello...

00:19:23.090 --> 00:19:24.760
It's too late now.

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:26.010
Get in here.

00:19:26.010 --> 00:19:27.840
Okay! Sorry to bother you!

00:19:28.970 --> 00:19:31.470
Well? What do you need?

00:19:31.630 --> 00:19:34.630
As Student Council President,
I am a very busy person.

00:19:34.630 --> 00:19:35.840
Make it quick.

00:19:36.130 --> 00:19:39.760
Right! I'd like to start a Jet Racing Club!

00:19:39.760 --> 00:19:42.090
In that case, you'll need to submit an application.

00:19:42.090 --> 00:19:43.300
Okay!

00:19:47.510 --> 00:19:51.050
According to this, you don't meet the
minimum requirement of five members.

00:19:51.050 --> 00:19:52.420
It's fine!

00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:54.260
How exactly is it fine?

00:19:56.010 --> 00:19:59.420
I figure everyone will join once the club gets started!

00:19:59.760 --> 00:20:00.760
Huh?

00:20:00.760 --> 00:20:02.170
I'm so excited!

00:20:06.470 --> 00:20:09.680
Why?! Why can't I have my club?!

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:41.590
Unfortunately, the road ahead would
prove to be dark and difficult...

00:20:42.010 --> 00:20:43.630
Join the Jet Racing Club!

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:45.800
Nope, not interested.

00:20:45.800 --> 00:20:47.800
Please! Join the Jet Racing Club!

00:20:47.800 --> 00:20:51.550
Sorry, I've got cram school in the afternoons.

00:20:52.920 --> 00:20:54.880
What's with the picture show?

00:20:54.880 --> 00:20:59.720
Back in Ojika, the kids next door
really loved this kind of stuff...

00:21:01.720 --> 00:21:02.720
Come on!

00:21:02.720 --> 00:21:06.340
Why ain't anyone joinin' my Jet Racing Club?!

00:21:06.340 --> 00:21:09.760
I even spent the whole day trying to recruit people...

00:21:10.470 --> 00:21:11.510
You're wasting your time.

00:21:11.510 --> 00:21:13.340
It's the middle of the semester.

00:21:13.340 --> 00:21:15.840
They've all joined other clubs.

00:21:15.840 --> 00:21:17.840
There has to be someone.

00:21:17.840 --> 00:21:20.670
Someone has to join my Jet Racing Club.

00:21:26.420 --> 00:21:27.470
I might...

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:30.380
have at least one person in mind...

00:21:30.380 --> 00:21:31.590
Really?!

00:21:35.800 --> 00:21:37.630
Y-Yeah...

00:21:38.130 --> 00:21:39.550
Misa-chan!

00:21:42.220 --> 00:21:44.840
I knew I could count on you!

00:21:45.720 --> 00:21:47.420
N-Namiki!

00:21:47.420 --> 00:21:49.470
Get off! Get out of my face!

00:21:49.880 --> 00:21:51.090
Cut it out!

00:21:52.870 --> 00:21:55.450
Let go of me already!

00:23:28.670 --> 00:23:29.670
It's mine.

00:23:29.670 --> 00:23:31.920
I absolutely must have it!

00:23:31.920 --> 00:23:33.340
Cut us some slack...

00:23:33.340 --> 00:23:35.380
I should never have said that!

00:23:35.380 --> 00:23:37.800
Misa-chan?

00:23:38.470 --> 00:23:40.970
I'm going to win...
